      "✅☑[C++/Java/Python/JavaScript] || 2 Approaches || EXPLAINED🔥 MarkSPhilip31 8500 1156 Nov 25, 2023 C++ Java Python3 C 3+ PLEASE UPVOTE IF IT HELPED \n \n Approaches \n (Also explained in the code) \n Approach 1(In-Built function) \n \n \n The  findWordsContaining  function searches through a vector of strings to identify words containing a specific character,  x . \n \n \n It iterates through each word in the input vector and counts occurrences of the character  x  within the word. \n \n \n If the count is greater than zero (i.e., if the character  x  is present in the word), it adds the index of that word to the result vector. \n \n \n Finally, it returns a vector containing indices of words that contain the specified character  x . \n \n \n Complexity \n \n \n Time complexity: \n O(n2)O(n^2) O ( n 2 ) \n \n \n Space complexity: \n O(1)O(1) O ( 1 ) \n \n \n Code \n C++ C Java Python3 JavaScript function   findWordsContaining ( words ,  x )   { \n      let  indices  =   [ ] ; \n      for   ( let  i  =   0 ;  i  <  words . length ;  i ++ )   { \n          if   ( words [ i ] . includes ( x ) )   { \n             indices . push ( i ) ; \n          } \n      } \n      return  indices ; \n } \n \n \n Approach 2(Greedy Approach) \n \n \n Function Objective: The function findWordsContaining searches for the character 'x' in each word of the input vector and records the indices of words containing 'x'. \n \n \n Input Parameters: \n \n \n \n vector& words:  The input vector containing a list of words. \n char x:  The character to be found in the words. \n \n \n Processing Steps: \n \n \n The function iterates through each word in the input vector. \n For each word, it iterates through each character to find if the character  x  exists within the word. \n When  x  is found in a word, the index of that word in the input vector is added to the result vector. \n The function returns a vector containing indices of  words  where  x  is found. \n \n \n Return Value: \n \n \n vector:  Contains indices of words that contain the character  x . \n \n Complexity \n \n \n Time complexity: \n O(n2)O(n^2) O ( n 2 ) \n \n \n Space complexity: \n O(1)O(1) O ( 1 ) \n \n \n Code \n C++ C Java Python3 JavaScript function   findWordsContaining ( words ,  x )   { \n      let  ans  =   [ ] ; \n \n      for   ( let  j  =   0 ;  j  <  words . length ;  j ++ )   { \n          let  temp  =  words [ j ] ; \n \n          for   ( let  i  =   0 ;  i  <  temp . length ;  i ++ )   { \n              if   ( temp [ i ]   ===  x )   { \n                 ans . push ( j ) ; \n                  break ; \n              } \n          } \n      } \n      return  ans ; \n } \n \n \n \n \n PLEASE UPVOTE IF IT HELPED \n \n \n Comments (1) lk-sai Apr 04, 2024 Can you explain how the time complexity is O(n2) in approach 1? I don't seem to understand that. 0 Reply",
