      "✅C++✅ C# ✅JavaScript.🔥Explained and very simple solutions for all.💯 aloneguy 472 464 May 10, 2023 C++ C# JavaScript Approach:First of all,we have to sort the given array from min to max.Pay attention,to collect the maximum number of coins we always choose 3 piles,which contains two maximum piles and minimum pile.It means we always get the second maximum amount after Alice. \n\n JavaScript C# C++ var   maxCoins   =   function ( piles )   { \n     piles . sort ( ( a , b ) => a - b ) ; \n       let  ans  =   0 ; \n          for   ( let  i  = 0 ,  j =  piles . length   - 2 ;  i  <  j ;  i ++ ,  j -= 2 ) \n         ans  +=  piles [ j ] ; \n          return  ans ;  \n } ; Comments (1) SMajumder2003 Nov 23, 2023 Easy solution, nice keep it up 0 Show 1 Replies Reply",
      "😎🚀 Beats 98% | Detailed Explaination 🔥🦅 | C++ | JAVA | PYTHON | JS Sanket_Deshmukh_07 889 766 Nov 23, 2023 C++ Java Python Python3 6+ Intuition \n UPVOTE IF YOU FOUND THIS HELPFUL !!! \n\n Approach \n \n SORT THE PILES VECTOR IN DECREASING ORDER. \n WE CAN TAKE ANY THREE NO.S SO HERE WE TAKE TWO LARGE NUMBERS FOR ALICE AND YOU, AND 1 SMALL NUMBER FOR BOB WHICH IS FROM ENDPOINT OF PILES VECTOR. \n FOR ALICE, JUST MOVE FORWARD THE POINTER i BY 1 \n FOR YOU, ADD THE VALUE TO ANSWER \n FOR BOB , DO j-- \n \n\n Complexity \n \n Time complexity: O(NlogN) \n \n\n \n Space complexity: O(1) \n \n\n Code \n class   Solution   { \n public : \n      int   maxCoins ( vector < int > &  piles )   { \n         ios_base :: sync_with_stdio ( false ) ; \n         cin . tie ( 0 ) ; \n         cout . tie ( 0 ) ; \n         \n          int  ans  =   0 ; \n          sort ( piles . begin ( ) , piles . end ( ) , greater < int > ( ) ) ; \n \n          int  i  =   0 ,  j  =  piles . size ( )   -   1 ; \n          while ( i  <  j ) \n          { \n             i ++ ;   // Alice \n             ans  +=  piles [ i ++ ] ;   // You \n             j -- ;   // Bob \n          } \n          return  ans ; \n      } \n } ; Comments (1) Hitesh_24 Nov 23, 2023 Nice Approach 2 Reply"
