      "[JavaScript] Elegant solution using a set and reduce (with explanation) mrhyde 224 2929 Jan 12, 2021 JavaScript Ordered Set It's a pretty straight forward solution. All we need to do is: \n \n create a set containing all allowed characters, \n iterate over all words using reduce accumulating the number of  good  words \n split each word into the array of letters \n check if  every  letter is present in a set of allowed words \n if so - increment the accumulator \n return accumulated value \n \n const   countConsistentStrings   =   ( allowed ,  words )   =>   { \n    let  set  =   new   Set ( allowed ) \n    return  words . reduce ( ( a ,  w )   =>   { \n      return  w . split ( '' ) . every ( l   =>  set . has ( l ) )   ?   ++ a  :  a\n    } ,   0 ) \n } Comments (7) uniqueorn Feb 23, 2022 6 Reply rbardini Dec 30, 2021 3 Reply ar2zee Feb 02, 2021 Why  ++a  and not  a++  I see that it's not working but I don't understand why ? 1 Show 2 Replies Reply yash2709 May 05, 2021 why making set of allowed? as it going to be always distinct? 0 Show 2 Replies Reply chanocuaalejandro Jun 22, 2022 What would be the time complexity? 0 Reply Siva56 Nov 16, 2021 brilliant 0 Reply dhtmlkitchen May 25, 2024 Read more -1 Show 1 Replies Reply",
      "All Solutions Short JavaScript Solution Using Regex sronin 348 1129 May 14, 2022 JavaScript Found these solution helpful? Consider showing support by upvoting this post. \nHave a question? Kindly leave a comment below. \nThank you and happy hacking! \n var   countConsistentStrings   =   function   ( allowed ,  words )   { \n      const  re  =   new   RegExp ( ` ^[ ${ allowed } ]+$ ` ) ; \n      let  count  =   0 \n \n     words . forEach ( word   =>   { \n          if   ( word . match ( re ) )  count ++ \n      } ) \n \n      return  count ; \n } ; Comments (0) No comments yet. 1 2 3 4 5 6 class   Solution  { public:      int   countConsistentStrings ( string   allowed ,  vector < string > &   words ) {              } }; Saved Ln 1, Col 1 You need to  Login / Sign up  to run or submit allowed = \"ab\" words = [\"ad\",\"bd\",\"aaab\",\"baa\",\"badab\"] 1 \"ab\" Source word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1",
