      "✅☑[C++/Java/Python/JavaScript] || Maps || EXPLAINED🔥 MarkSPhilip31 8512 1129 Oct 28, 2023 C++ Java Python3 C 2+ PLEASE UPVOTE IF IT HELPED \n \n Approaches \n (Also explained in the code) \n \n \n The  sumCounts  function takes a vector of integers  nums  as input and calculates the sum of the squares of the sizes of all possible distinct subsequences. \n \n \n It uses a map named  mp  to store unique elements within each subarray. \n \n \n The variable  sum  is initialized to 0, which will store the final result. \n \n \n The function iterates over all subarrays of the input array using two nested loops. The outer loop specifies the starting index  i , and the inner loop specifies the ending index  j . \n \n \n Within the inner loop, it iterates from index  i  to  j  and inserts each element into the map  mp . \n \n \n After processing all elements in the current subarray, it calculates the square of the map's size and adds it to the  sum . \n \n \n The map is then cleared to be used for the next subarray. \n \n \n Finally, the function returns the total  sum , which represents the sum of the squares of the sizes of all distinct subsequences. \n \n \n Complexity \n \n \n Time complexity: \n O(n3)O(n^3) O ( n 3 ) \n \n \n Space complexity: \n O(n)O(n) O ( n ) \n \n \n Code \n C++ C Java Python3 JavaScript class   Solution   { \n      sumCounts ( nums )   { \n          const  mp  =   new   Map ( ) ; \n          let  sum  =   0 ; \n \n          for   ( let  i  =   0 ;  i  <  nums . length ;  i ++ )   { \n              for   ( let  j  =  i ;  j  <  nums . length ;  j ++ )   { \n                  let  a  =  i ; \n                  while   ( a  <=  j )   { \n                     mp . set ( nums [ a ] ,   0 ) ; \n                     a ++ ; \n                  } \n                 sum  +=  mp . size   **   2 ; \n                 mp . clear ( ) ; \n              } \n          } \n          return  sum ; \n      } \n } \n \n \n PLEASE UPVOTE IF IT HELPED \n \n \n Comments (1) KondalDurgam Feb 01, 2024 Where is the javascript solution why do you add a javascript tag? 0 Show 1 Replies Reply",
