      "Javascript Easiest solution. Muhsin-42 11 278 May 30, 2023 JavaScript Intuition \n The code appears to aim at finding the maximum sum by selecting the maximum element from the given array nums and adding k consecutive integers starting from 0. \n Approach \n \n Find the maximum element in the array using Math.max(...nums). \n Initialize the variable sum with the maximum element. \n Iterate k-1 times starting from 1 (since we have already accounted for 0 in the maximum element). \n In each iteration, add the current maximum element plus the current iteration index to the sum. \n Return the final sum. \n \n Complexity \n \n Time complexity: O(k) \n \n\n \n Space complexity: O(1) \n \n\n Code \n  \n var   maximizeSum   =   function ( nums ,  k )   { \n      let  max  =   Math . max ( ... nums ) ; \n     sum  =  max ; \n      for ( let  i = 1 ;  i < k ;  i ++ ) { \n         sum +=  max + i ; \n      } \n      return  sum ; \n } ; Comments (1) whales70 Jun 20, 2023 Math.max(...nums) takes O(n) time to run so the solution would be O(n+k) time 0 Show 1 Replies Reply",
