      "All Solutions ✅Beats 98.65% with just 2 lines of code😱 | step by step explanation🔥 SumitPokhriyal 95 76 Jun 04, 2023 JavaScript TypeScript Array Greedy <img src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/users/images/a9af8941-e4e0-48a3-a1f0-39d303cb6539_1685936382.6902094.png\" alt=\"Screenshot (19).png\"> \n Intuition \n\n The problem requires finding the maximum possible sum by performing a specific operation on the given array of numbers. \n Approach \n\n \n \n let max = Math.max(...nums); - This line finds the maximum number in the nums array using the Math.max function and the spread operator (...). It spreads the array elements as individual arguments to the Math.max function, which returns the maximum value. \n \n \n return ((max + k) * (max + k - 1)/2) - (max * (max - 1) / 2 ); - This line performs the calculation to maximize the sum. It calculates the sum of consecutive numbers from 1 to the new maximum number (max + k) and subtracts the sum of consecutive numbers from 1 to the original maximum number (max). \n \n \n (max + k) * (max + k - 1)/2 calculates the sum of consecutive numbers from 1 to max + k. This is done using the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series. \n \n \n (max * (max - 1) / 2) calculates the sum of consecutive numbers from 1 to max. \n \n \n By subtracting the sum of the original range from the sum of the new range, the code obtains the difference between the two ranges, which represents the maximum possible increase in the sum. \n \n \n \n \n Complexity \n \n Time complexity: O(n) - The code has a linear time complexity as it iterates through the array to find the maximum number. \n Space complexity: O(1) - The code has a constant space complexity as it does not use additional space that grows with the input size; it only utilizes a few scalar variables. \n \n Code \n function maximizeSum ( nums :  number [ ] ,  k :  number ) :  number  { \n     let  max   =  Math . max ( . . . nums ) ; \n      return   ( ( max   +  k )   *   ( max   +  k  -   1 ) / 2 )   -   ( max   *   ( max   -   1 )   /   2   ) \n } ; Comments (0) No comments yet. 1 2 3 4 5 6 class   Solution  { public:      int   maximizeSum ( vector < int > &   nums ,  int   k ) {              } }; Saved Ln 1, Col 1 You need to  Login / Sign up  to run or submit nums = [1,2,3,4,5] k = 3 1 [1,2,3,4,5] Source word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1"
